{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the anger of YHWH burned against Moshe.</b> Every place where חרון אף (burning anger) is written concerning the Holy One, blessed be He, leaves a mark, and here He left a mark upon him. This is what the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: that the priesthood was taken from him, and this is what is meant by הלא אהרן אחיך הלוי — 'is not Aharon your brother the Levi,' that is, he is designated in your place for the priesthood. And they further expounded on this that He left a mark in that he was never healed. And it would have been possible for Him to do him the honor of healing him, just as He did him the honor with the radiance of the skin of his face, and this is the mark — that He did not heal him. And so they expounded: הלא אהרן אחיך הלוי — 'is not Aharon your brother the Levi,' ידעתי כי דבר ידבר הוא — 'I know that he will surely speak' — but you shall never be healed." "<b>And he will see you and rejoice in his heart.</b> They were not envious of one another's greatness. This is what Scripture says (Psalms 133:1): הנה מה טוב ומה נעים שבת אחים גם יחד. And it does not say שמח בפיו but rather בלבו. R. Shimon ben Yochai said: the heart that rejoices in the greatness of its brother — the Urim and Tummim shall rest upon it, as it is said: והיו על לב אהרן — 'and they shall be upon the heart of Aharon.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:07.004669335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}